Oh, yes, I agree that you can share all memory resources from the
level 1 cache onwards - 'conventional' (i.e. modern SMP) doesn't
start before level 2, though earlier designs used to.  But you
can't share most of the thread context (e.g. registers, flags and
mode) - and, in the Itanic's case, those total 4 KB.

