>make TLB sharing meaningful in an SMT context.  Great care is needed,
>*of course* -- madness lies in not taking great care.  No disagreement.

I was actually thinking of the multiple mode problem.  TLB misses
and the simpler forms of page fault can be handled in a completely
interrupt-disabled kernel thread, but you can't handle real page
faults like that.  Nor can you allow the calling of most kernel
functions without adding vast extra complexity.


