  It has been a long time, but I think if you push the Fault button when
it is lit, all the panel lights will flash in a pattern giving the error
code (this only works if no bulbs are burned out 8-).

  You can also open the top of the drive and find the DB-25 serial con-
nector and hook up a terminal to it. It is either 300, 1200, or 2400 baud
(I forget). Make sure none of the front panel buttons (start, A, or B) are
pushed in. Type a ^C on the terminal to wake it up. You should get a ">>>"
prompt. You can then say "RUN DIAG" to exercise the drive. If it passes,
start the drive and do another "RUN DIAG".

