Interestingly, what killed the 68K architecture was the serial decoding
of some instructions, which made superscalar 68K MPUs (68060) a
nightmare to design, the 68060 was late and underperformed. 

It would be perfectly possible to build a modern 68K with a tracecache
that wouldn't suffer from this instruction decode bottleneck (well to
some degree anyway).

