Darryl,

There were three models of main logic boards (motherboards) made by
DEC for the DECpc XL chassis, later re-christened Celebris XL.  I
forget the DEC part numbers of the first two, but the third one
carries DEC part number 54-23606 and it was used in the Celebris XL.

The part number is etched on the board along with the circuitry.  You
can find it along the left hand edge of the board, looking down on the
main logic board from the front.

The first ever DECpc XL main logic board does not support Pentium
CPUs.  The second one does, up to 133MHz.  The third one supports up
to a dual 166 or single 200.

You need a processor card with Socket 5 CPU sockets.  The latest and
last processor card is 54-24490. 

I have all this kit for sale here, but it would cost a small fortune
to ship to the other side of the planet... Ben Myers

