I've seen a 32 MB set with boards numbered 5021138-01 (on the board
itself) and a stick-on label: 5421139CP.  32 MB memory sets (8 x 4 MB)
have memory chips on only 1 side of the SIMM.

I've also seen a 64 MB set with SIMM boards numbered the same:
5021138-01.  The stick-on label says: 5421139DP.  (The suffix is DP
instead of CP.)  These SIMMS have memory chips on both sides.

Alas, I didn't write down any chip part numbers on these SIMMs.

I've seen 256 MB kits from Viking and Dataram, but they don't have similar
numbering.

If you have a working 3000/600, the easiest thing would be to ask the
computer to identify the memory for you.

