When the system powers up, it does a self-test that includes the keyboard
and mouse:

DEC 3000 - M600
Digital Equipment Corporation
System conducting power up tests
------------------------------------------------------------

Devnam           Devstat
--------         -------
     CPU          OK KN17-BA -V7.0-S887-I21F-sV2.1-DECchip 21064  P3.0
     OSC          175 MHz
    ASIC          OK
     MEM          OK 320MB
     NVR          OK
     SCC          OK ptr(0) = Not Present  keybd(2) = Not Present

The line above says the SCC (Serial Communications Controller) is ok, but
there is no keyboard or mouse.  If they had been present, it would have
tested them as well.  The power-up sequence continues...

      NI          OK Ethernet Address: 08-00-2B-92-85-B6 , TENBT
    SCSI          OK
    ISDN          OK
     TC2          OK - PMAD-AA
     TC1          OK - KZTSA-AA
     TC0          OK - PMAGB-BA

Do you get a good power-up display?

