Configuration
  a.. Four memory motherboards (MMB) mount on the system module. To have an
operational memory subsystem, all four MMB's must be present
  b.. The memory arrays are spread among the four MMB's. Each bank of memory
consists of eight memory modules, two on each MMB.
  c.. A bank represents the eight memory arrays (memory modules 0 through 7)
  d.. The banks are numbered 0 through 7, with 0 being closest to the CPU
module.
  e.. A slot consists of two banks because every memory array can be
populated on both sides.
Rules
  a.. Each memory bank must be filled in sets of eight memory modules.
  b.. The eight memory SIMMs in a bank must be of equal size.
  c.. The eight memory SIMMs in a bank must be of the same type. They must
all be single or double sided



