Those are not SCSI controllers, but "personality modules". In fact they act
as SCSI bridges between the cabinet and the SCSI controller in the system.

If I'm not mistaken (!!) the following types exist:

2 high density connectors in a 90 degree angle = SE wide.
2 ultra high density connectors next to each other: split bus UWSE (2 SCSI
busses in one 365 cabinet)
1 ultra high density connector UWSE
1 high density connector : Diff SCSI.> UWSE

Blue cabinets are always UWSE on the backplane.

I don't know what the dipswitches do, I have never seen that their settings
were changed.

regards,

Dirk

