In article <tivutmge6q3m5b@corp.supernews.com>, "Raptorfan" <raptorfan@earthlink.net> writes:
>THANK YOU. This is a damn sight more info than I've been able to find in the
>last 2+ months. The cabinets I'm using are older than blue.. they're MacPlus
>Beige. Judging from your info I have SE Wide controllers. Would still like
>to know the exact designations for the DIPs (I think there are 7-8 total;
>I'm thinking 4 are ID, 1-2 are some sort of termination (what I REALLY want
>to know) and the others are mystery). I have a 6(?)-high cabinet.

Pull the controller out of the StorageWorks cabinet and look at the bottom
for the part number.  If it is 70-31490-01, the switches set the base SCSI
address for the drives in the cabinet.  Since a wide configuration supports
16 addresses, you can have your 7 StorageWorks slots appear at an arbitrary
starting address.  Count binary from the first switch designated (1) of the
7 total.

