  Nope, no tapes are supported on shared SCSI.  Not directly, and not 
  behind an HSZ controller.  (The HSZ firmware passes through the SCSI 
  reset, meaning the tape can/will unexpectedly rewind.  I know of one
  site that tried this, and the SCSI reset wedged access to the tape on
  the other system, and required a reboot to again permit tape access.)

:If anyone has other useful info I'd appreciate hearing about it. 

  Serve the tape to another host via TMSCP, or (better) share or serve 
  the disk to the host with the tape?  If you need/want a tape drive in 
  a multi-host/shared-bus configuration, you're left with stuff like 
  Fibre Channel, CI, MDR.  Or the DSSI/TF series stuff, for those folks
  with an interest in older buses and older storage widgets...

