> Not the BIOS, the SRM console. And it won't help.

It's the first step. Go to:

    http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/readmes/as800.html

and download (and apply) the firmware update if your DS3305 is not
already at V5.8.

Once the machine is running the current SRM/ARC firmware you will need
to set the following environmental variables to these values from the
SRM console:

    >>> set os_type openvms (or unix)
    >>> set boot_reset on

You will also need to edit the nvram script and add the following
lines:

    >>> edit nvram

    (a ? inside the editor will show you the editor commands)

    10 set srm_boot on
    20 e

The line numbers will different if your nvram script already contains
commands. You can view the contents of the nvram file by:

   >>> cat nvram

Once you have changed the environment as above initialize the
system with:

   >>> init

Now your DS3305 should be able to boot either OpenVMS or Tru64.

