As has been pointed out the license allows running them on an emulator,
however, it should be noted that it is only allowed on *one* emulator. 
Specifically simh.

As for RSX-11* there is no publically available copy avaialable for simh,
even though RSX-11M and M+ are permited.  Nor are any of the layered
products that are permited available.  It should also be noted that the
license is only good up to a certain version.  For example, the current
version of RT-11 is V5.7, but the license is only good through V5.3. 
Layered products are good through current as of the last release allowed for
the OS which they run on.

For more details please refer to the license document itself.

For information on simh and what software is actually available for it
please refer to the home site for simh:
http://www.tiac.net/users/mps/retro/

			Zane


