Look for another VS3100m76.  I saw one or two rather recently for auction
on eBay.  I didn't follow the auction so I can't report on the final bid
price.  I'd guess it wan't too much though.

>  Is my hardware FUBAR?

There is no UNIBUS in a VS3100m76.  :)


>  Memory swapping hasn't
>helped.  

Take the unit apart and carefully blow the years of accumulated dust and
crud out of the cabinet.  You will need to remove the disk drive mounting
plate to expose the main PCB below it to clean it properly.  If this unit
did work prior to shelving it for several months, it could just be dirt.
Worth a try?

Oxides can also build on the component lead which are not soldered to the
board.  I had a VS3100m76 which sat dormant for upward of a year and the
solder pads on the memory oxidized.  I carefully removed them and cleaned
them with a PCB cleaner chemical.  Ne'er a problem since.
 
