We're getting our first chance in a while to quote a new cluster
configuration, replacing a standalone VAX.  We've been asked if there
is a way to provide a shared tape drive (essentially, a drive on a
shared SCSI bus) for the two Alphas without going to fiber channel.  I
know you can't do it on a plain shared bus, and I've not been able to
locate documentation that says how to do it with current equipment,
but I also know it was possible to serve certain DLT drives with the
HSZ40-era controllers (at least its documented there; we never tried
it).

So, short of going to fiber, can it be done in a VMScluster?  If not
we'll likely stick with SCSI and put one drive on each system (which
has its own benefits anyway).

Also noted: the DS20E supported options currently have a caveat on the
KZPBA-CA adapter; if a TLZ10 is installed on it that no disks can by
placed on the same bus.  A DS10 with a TLZ10 and an internal SCSI disk
ends up needing two KZP adapters, suing up two slots... I don't think
this caveat used to be there; we have one early DS10 system that came
configured from Compaq with a TLZ10 and two internal drives on the
single KZPBA-CA, and have no issues with it, or complaints from the
service contract folks.

Thanks in advance for any information.

Rich Jordan
CCS


