In article <cc5619f2.0106151313.26002f5b@posting.google.com>, jordan@ccs4vms.com (Rich Jordan) writes:
:...We've been asked if there is a way to provide a shared tape drive 
:(essentially, a drive on a shared SCSI bus) for the two Alphas without 
:going to fiber channel...

  Served tapes -- initially including TMSCP tapes and then later adding 
  served SCSI tape support -- been available for a while now...

:I know you can't do it on a plain shared bus...

  The "fun" with tapes on a shared SCSI bus has to do with the occasional
  SCSI resets that can (and do) occur.  SCSI disks (withg TCQ support) 
  recover nicely from the reset, but tapes tend to (correctly) rewind,
  and this sudden loss of positioning has "interesting" side-effects...

	--

  Often, the easiest approach is to configure the disks on the shared 
  SCSI, and use the system with the local tape drive for the BACKUP 
  from these disks...


