Not related to your cache question, but I see a few other improvements
that you could make:

(1) About half of your contri[i] values are set to zero just above this
code.  Add a test to avoid doing the inner loop at all when this is true.

(2) Similarly, many of iso_coefs[j] values are zero.  Unroll the
N_ISOSPIN loop by hand and omit those calculations.

(3) Look at the assembly code to see if your compiler optimizes 
iso_ff[i][j][IM] into something reasonable.  If not, convert iso_ff into
a single-dimensional array and do the address calculations by hand.


