You can find electronic documentation for the Celebris XL-6200 at

http://www4.service.digital.com/documentation/pcdoc/celxl6.htm

The Service Maintenance Manual is sd_cexl.pdf .  The same manual
covers both XL-6xxx and XL-5xxx (classic Pentium) models.

Memory has to be fast-page mode 72-pin with parity.  Non-parity memory
will not work.  Newer EDO memory will not work.  SIMMs must be
installed in matched sets.  With the XL-6200, you do not install
memory on the main logic board.  Instead, use the SIMM sockets on the
processor card.  See the Service Maintenance Manual for more details.

Not sure about FreeBSD, but Linux works on these computers.

... Ben Myers

