In article <RiOS6.3879$Ib.418149@news1.primary.net>, "Jack Peacock" <peacock@simconv.com> writes:
:I recently obtained a TLZ06 4mm DAT drive but I'm not clear on the
:capacity of this drive.  Is it a DDS or DDS-2? 

  DDS-1, IIRC.

:Will it take 120 meter tapes?

  No.  90m is the limit for TLZ06.

  TLZ04    60m (DDS-1)
  TLZ06    60m, 90m (DDS-1)
  TLZ07    60m, 90m (DDS-1); 120m (DDS-2)
  TLZ09    60m, 90m (DDS-1); 120m (DDS-2)
  TLZ10    60m, 90m (DDS-1); 120m (DDS-2); 125m (DDS-3)

  Do NOT use a longer cartridge than the DDS (DAT) drive supports.
  (More tape media is NOT better for backups, in this particular case...)

