This may be an easy fix.
    The internal leader on the takup spool is probably disconnected and has
wound back into the
unit takeup reel.  you need to remove the TK70 , remove the 3 philips screws
that hold the
metal cover at the top rear of the drive that covers the takeup reel and
data head.  Carefully thread the mylar
leader past the tape head and attach the leader to the hook and lever near
the left  middle of the
unit.  The leader has an end that looks like a spade or anchor , just behind
this is the square
hole that the plastic hook/lever   locks into.  The hook/lever pivits on a
spring ,. Carefully pull it back to
allow for it to hook into the leader's hole . Once hooked the leader is
ready to grab another tape.
This is a common problem on all DTL tapes .Check you last tape used , open
the flap to see if its leader is damaged . There should be  a loop exposed
at the edge of the door.  You need to defeat a few interlocks to
open a cassette door. Helps to have 3 hands  :)

brian.



